     "head": "SportsUNIT 5 This unit introduces students to the wide and exciting world of sports and physical activities, highlighting their importance in maintaining a healthy and active lifestyle. It begins by focusing on India’s rich heritage of indigenous martial arts such as Thang-Ta, which combines body movements, breathing techniques, and weapon skills to develop physical control and mental balance. These traditional practices reflect cultural values and promote discipline and self-defence. The unit further explores various tr aditional Indian sport and martial arts like Mallakhamb, Gatka, and Kalaripayattu. These activities not only improve strength, flexibility, and coordination but also teach focus, courage, and respect. They serve as an important link between physical training and cultural traditions, helping students understand the significance of India’s historical sporting practices. In"
    },
