     "head": "music नादेन व््यज््यते वर््णणः पदं वर्ा्णत्पदाद्वचणः । वचसो व््यवहारोऽ्यं नादाधीनमतो जगत् ॥२॥ Nādena vyajyate varṇaḥ padaṁ varṇāt padād vachaḥ| Vachaso vyavahāroʼyaṁ nādādhīnamato jagat||2|| – Saṅgītaratnākara, Svarādhyāya, Ch. 2 Meaning: Nāda manifests the letters (of the alphabet), letters constitute the word, and words make a sentence. So, the entire business of life is carried on through language, and therefore, the whole phenomenon (that is, the world) is based on nāda. Guru–Śhiṣhya playing bansuri 6_Ch6 Music.indd 876_Ch6 Music.indd 87 05-05-2026 4.57.30 PM05-05-2026 4.57.30 PM"
    },
    {
     "file": "iemr107",
     "pages": 8,
     "head": "7 The Science of Music Music is both an art and a science. This means that you can enjoy music for the various emotions it invokes and for the entertainment and relaxation it provides, but equally, you can also study it in-depth. Also, music is connected to various aspects of our lives and the different subjects that we study in school. In this chapter , we will explore how music is connected to physics, biology, and maths. Fig. 7.4. Mṛidaṅgam Fig. 7.1. Chimṭā Fig. 7.2. Flute Fig. 7.3. Santoor Note to the teacher: When you are teaching this chapter , at the beginning of each period, play a recording of a musical instrument from various categories—string (tata-vādya), wind (suṣhira-vādya), percussion (avanaddha-vādya) and solid (ghana-vādya). Encourage children to identify the category that the instrument belongs to. 7_Ch7 Music.indd 1037_Ch7 Music.indd 103 05-05-2026 5.08.39 PM05-05-202"
    },
    {
     "file": "iemr108",
     "pages": 16,
     "head": "Rāga and Tāla8 Let us recall Nāda: Musical sound Śhruti: A sound that is heard clearly and can be recognised as distinct from another Svara: A note in music. There are seven notes in Indian music— S R G M P D N Saptak/ Sthāyī: An octave or register in music. Musicians usually perform in Mandra (lower), Madhya (middle) and Tāra (higher) saptak/ octaves. Svara Let us revisit some of the basic building blocks of melody in classical music.  There are 7 notes (svaras) of music.  S and P are the invariant notes known as achala-svara/ prakṛiti-svara.  The remaining 5 notes (R G M D N) have higher and lower variants and known as chala-svaras/ vikṛiti-svaras.  So, the total number of notes (svara-sthānas) comprise 2 prakṛiti-svaras or achala-svaras (S and P), and 2 variants of the remaining 5 notes (R G M D N), bringing the total number of note positions to 12. In a keyboard or a harmonium, y"
    },
    {
     "file": "iemr109",
     "pages": 8,
     "head": "Music Travels Around the World 9 Have you travelled to a town, city, or country different from where you live? Just as human beings travel and move from one place to another , music and culture also flow between different regions and countries. So, let’s pack our bags and set off on a journey! Music and Migration Migration is the movement of people from one place to another to settle in a new location. When populations such as people of a country or an ethnic group that originated from the same place settle in a new country, they form what is called a diaspora. Over thousands of years, people moved in and out of the Indian subcontinent. And, with them, they carried not just physical possessions, but also their music. The music they carried served many purposes — it provided links to their home, helped them bond with fellow migrants, preserved their cultural practices, and also allowed th"
    },
    {
     "file": "iemr110",
     "pages": 19,
     "head": "Dance आङ् गिको वागिकस््तद््वदाहार््य यः सागत्वकस््तथा। ि्तुर्ा्यगिनर्ो ह्येषयः ि्तुद््य्वीपव्तीं महीम्।। नाट्यशास्त्र, अध्याय 6, 38 Āṅgiko vāchikas tadvad āhāryaḥ sāttvikastathā | Chaturdhābhinayo hyeṣhaḥ chaturdvīpavatīṁ mahīm|| Nāṭyaśhāstra, Chapter 6, 38 Meaning: Abhinaya is four-fold — āṅgika (body gestures), vāchika (speech/ vocals), āhārya (costumes and make-up), and sāttvika (mental states/ emotions). Traditional folk dance forms of Tamil Nadu potraying Poikā l Kudirai, Oyilāttam, and Silambāttam 10_Ch10 Dance.indd 13510_Ch10 Dance.indd 135 05-05-2026 4.08.34 PM05-05-2026 4.08.34 PM"
    },
    {
     "file": "iemr111",
     "pages": 6,
     "head": "Dance as Visual Storytelling11 Many Indian dance forms are deeply rooted in the tradition of storytelling. Often described as dṛiśhya-kāvya, or visual poetry, Indian dance uses movement, gesture, and facial expression to communicate meaning clearly and powerfully. Through this expressive tradition, dancers bring to life a wide range of narratives — from classical literary works such as Kālidāsa’s Abhijñāna-Śhākuntalam to modern interpretations of Shakespeare’s Romeo and Juliet; the rhythms of seasonal cycles and the journey from sowing seeds to harvest, scenes from everyday life, and the lived experiences of people. In the previous chapter , we saw examples of the four types of abhinayas. The integrated use of abhinayas in dance allows for the emotion and intent to be transmitted to the audience. Let us creatively explore Āṅgika, Vāchika, and Āhārya Abhinayas! Fig. 11.1. Romeo and Juliet"
    },
    {
     "file": "iemr112",
     "pages": 9,
     "head": "12 Cultural Connections Through Dance Culture connects people beyond boundaries. Our customs, social traditions, regional ideas, and beliefs together shape our culture. People from different cultures can connect and develop mutual respect through shared appreciation of diverse dance traditions. For example, dance forms like Dandiya and Bhangra have travelled beyond our borders with the Indian diaspora and are now being enjoyed across the world. They are no longer limited to a single community and have become part of the wider local culture wherever they are performed. Indian dance forms have also been adopted by international dancers promoting cross-cultural relations. Fig. 12.1. The global presence of Bhangra (1) Flashmobs in Birmingham; (2) Half-time performances at NBA games in the USA; (3) Stage competitions in Singapore; and (4) Lohri celebrations in Punjab 1 2 3 4 12_Ch 12 Dance.in"
    },
    {
     "file": "iemr113",
     "pages": 10,
     "head": "13 Dance Choreography Just as a river’s flow is directed around rocks and pebbles, choreography shapes the way a dance flows. Choreography is the art of creating and arranging dance movements to form a visual pattern or spectacle. The placement of dancers, their directions, pauses, and movements are decisions choreographers make to bring their vision to life. Do you know? The first known thinker on the idea of choreography in India is Sage Bhārata, the author of the Nāṭyaśhāstra. More than 2000 years ago, he described a concept called ‘Piṇḍībandhas’, which are group formations characterised by clustering, weaving, linking, and moving in coordinated shapes. Many of these ancient ideas appear in choreographies even today, such as:  group formations and shapes;  coordinated travelling patterns; and  movement flow in unison or in opposition. Choreography and Collaboration In the context o"
    },
    {
     "file": "iemr114",
     "pages": 14,
     "head": "सत्यंं च वैैणि�कंं चैवै नाागरंं णि�श्र�ेवै च । णिचत्रंं चतुुणिवैिधंं प्रोोक्तंं तुस्यं वैक्ष्यंाणि� लक्ष��् ॥ १ ॥ – विष््णणुधर्मोत्तरपणुरा्ण, 41.1 Satyaṁ cha vaiṇikaṁ chaiva nāgaraṁ miśhrameva cha | Chitraṁ chatur-vidhaṁ proktaṁ tasya vakṣhyāmi lakṣhaṇam || 1 || – Viṣhṇu-dharmottara Purāṇa, 41.1 Meaning: According to Chapter 41, Volume 1 of the ‘Chitra-sūtra’ in the Viṣhṇu-dharmottara Purāṇa, there are four types of paintings: Satya (Realistic),Vaiṇika (Classical/ Lyrical), Nāgara (Urban/ Refined), and Miśhra (Mixed). I shall now describe their characteristics. Visual Arts Image depicting life in a city 14_Ch 14 VA.indd 17914_Ch 14 VA.indd 179 05-05-2026 5.16.49 PM05-05-2026 5.16.49 PM"
    },
    {
     "file": "iemr115",
     "pages": 15,
     "head": "Now that you have gone through the essential warm-up activities like sketching and journalling, get ready for exploring the next level of Visual Art. The choice of materials, tools, and techniques has shaped every artist’s expression throughout history. Think of the range of surfaces and materials from the prehistoric cave paintings made with earth pigments to the digital drawing devices of today! Many artworks have survived changing weather and climatic conditions as well as other external threats and damage. The fact that we can still see and experience artworks that were made thousands of years ago proves that artists had deep knowledge and advanced techniques of using various materials in art processes. Let us recall Some pottery and metal casting techniques that are practised today are more than 5,000 years old. Talking About Mediums The word ‘medium’ is a common term that refers to"
    },
    {
     "file": "iemr116",
     "pages": 9,
     "head": "Composition is a term used across art forms. A good visual composition is created when the elements of art are arranged by applying the principles of visual design. Compositions can be either two-dimensional, like paintings and textiles, or three-dimensional, like free-standing sculptures, installations, and reliefs.  The terms ‘realistic’ or ‘naturalistic’ are used for artworks where the images resemble objects, nature, and people as they appear in reality.  The term ‘abstract’ is used to describe artworks which are imaginative creations, which may not have any direct resemblance to objects seen in reality.  Some compositions are a combination of both naturalistic and abstract imagery. Discussion circle Discuss the elements that make a composition in Theatre, Music, and Dance. Fig. 16.1. ‘There comes Papa’ by Raja Ravi Varma, Oil on canvas, 1893 Look at these examples and relate them"
    },
    {
     "file": "iemr117",
     "pages": 7,
     "head": "The Visual Arts comprise a broad range of art and design practices. When people say that they are visual artists, it is usually followed up with the question, ‘What kind of visual arts?’ In this chapter you will learn about the many branches of Visual Arts and get a brief insight into the respective careers relating to each of these branches. Note to the teacher: Encourage students to explore types of Visual Arts that they are interested in. Assign groups to enquire about each branch mentioned here. For the benefit of the entire class, a presentation can be made by each group. Branches of Visual Arts17 Fig. 17.1. Some major disciplines in Visual Arts Painting Sculpture Digital Art Print Making Photography Heritage Crafts 17_Ch 17 VA.indd 21717_Ch 17 VA.indd 217 01-05-2026 4.00.57 PM01-05-2026 4.00.57 PM"
    }
